  "body": "Defaults to `True`.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/50022cff966a3991fbd8a1e5c98f490d9b335442/tests/rest/client/utils.py#L51\r\n\r\nDocstring says:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/50022cff966a3991fbd8a1e5c98f490d9b335442/tests/rest/client/utils.py#L65-L67\r\n\r\nBut the only use is:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/50022cff966a3991fbd8a1e5c98f490d9b335442/tests/rest/client/utils.py#L80-L81\r\n\r\nMoreover, the CS spec [says](https://spec.matrix.org/unstable/client-server-api/#post_matrixclientr0createroom) of `visibility` that\r\n\r\n> Rooms default to private visibility if this key is not included.\r\n\r\nSuggest:\r\n\r\n- Change is_public to `Optional[bool]`, default `None`\r\n- `if is_public is False`, set visibility to private\r\n- `elif is_public is True`, set visibility to public\r\n- else do nothing.\r\n\r\nCould alternatively leave it as a bool and fix it to actually set visibility to public when True. That would probably require fixing a bunch of tests to explicitly set `is_public`: False.\r\n\r\nSpotted by @AndrewFerr in #10930.",
